    "body": "progress (issue-worker-high): local commits on `issue/689-step-chord-cap`. The quick gate is running; the branch is not pushed yet.\n\n- 32156f18: mkinney's held chord cap, cherry-picked (STEP chord target `min(extent/1000, DEV_TOL/2)`).\n- e5417aa8: the arc fit and the arc reading now leave the mesh its share of the 0.01 mm verdict.\n  - `fit_arcs`: a replaced vertex must stand within tol/2 of the fitted circle. On the solid_law contour the R35 centre error drops from (0.027, -0.040) to (0.004, -0.006) mm.\n  - `fit_arcs`: a closing ring takes its turning direction from its signed area. A regular rim was read backwards, so it ended on a chord. On the Ø25 hole that chord made the lead-out cross the ring: 9 `Crossing` findings, which appear once the gouges are gone.\n  - Verify law (b) reads arc moves at tol/4 instead of tol. The verdict is unchanged. At tol, the inscribed chords convicted nominal arcs round convex walls (4 gouges in shoulder_adaptive) and hid real gouge on concave walls.\n- cd5c3885: 9 golden_cl goldens regenerated (arc-fit only).\n\nTargeted readings: bore_facet_sagitta 2/2, solid_law, lead_approach, level_links, wall_arc_entry, shoulder_adaptive, golden_cl, arcs and import all pass.\n",
