    "body": "Review round 1 on PR #839 is fixed on `issue/689-step-chord-cap`, head bb71d19d (merged with origin/main 72ab8fdb).\n\n- **Merge and goldens.** The only golden main's new code moved is the Doosan DNM contour pair (`nc/doosan-dnm/contour_{disc_hole,tangential_lead}.nc`), from the arc fit. Its diff is byte-for-byte the Fanuc one. It is regenerated in its own commit (18c30494). Trochoid, plasma, microARC, fixture plates and mod vises moved no golden.\n- **Gouge-law flip, named and pinned.** The PR body now says in plain words that the quarter arc reading turns some former gouges into passes and some former passes into gouges. Both directions are pinned against the analytic distance in the new `verify_arc_reading` suite:\n  - a nominal arc round a convex wall now passes (true clearance 4.998 against a 4.99 floor; the old chords read 4.988);\n  - arcs cut 15 µm past the floor round a convex wall and inside a concave wall are convicted under both readings;\n  - an arc bowing 5 µm past the floor into a straight wall, which the old chords hid, is now convicted.\n\n  With the share set back to 1.0, exactly the two flip tests fail.\n- **`wall_arc_entry`.** It now pins literal counts: 5 bore arc entries and 8 plunges.\n- **Figures corrected.** The `contour_disc_hole` lead-out end moves 2.12 mm (I had written 1.4), and every other \"moved by\" figure is re-measured.\n- **STEP timing.** Milling-test.step goes from 448 to 952 facets (14 to 27 ms). sample_ap214.step, the largest STEP in testdata, stays at 1550. The facet budget bound (`budget / 8` per pass, about 15 M kept, 30 M cap) is named in the PR body. `arc_leads.rs` gains its provenance line.\n- **Gate.** The full quick gate is green on bb71d19d (45 min): sim, motion and app. All sim test binaries pass, and clippy `-D warnings` is clean on motion, sim and app.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
