    "body": "Review round 2 on PR #839 is fixed, head 7de81044.\n\n- **Over-budget STEP mesh, both directions.** The PR body and the decision file now name both:\n  - a concave wall can show a false gouge (the safe side);\n  - a convex wall can pass a real gouge up to the mesh's actual chord error (the unsafe side).\n\n  This PR does not introduce the risk. I verified in `step.rs` that every mesh is at least as fine as before: the new target is never above the old `extent/1000`, and the pass sequence is identical up to the old target. The PR removes the risk for every model within the facet budget. The over-budget case is tracked in #864.\n- **Chord clamp.** `MAX_ARC_CHORDS` (1024) binds the quarter arc reading above r ~ 531 mm for a full circle; the old reading hit it above r ~ 2125 mm. Above that radius the quarter reading degrades toward the old one, never past it. This is pinned by `verify_arc_reading::the_quarter_reading_is_never_coarser_than_the_old_one_at_any_radius`.\n- **Checks run.** `verify_arc_reading` passes 5/5, and clippy `-D warnings` on camcraft-app is clean. The full quick gate was green on bb71d19d; this round adds tests and docs only.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
