    "body": "Review round 3 on PR #839 is fixed, head 9c5d869c. The unit finding is **confirmed**: `step.rs` tessellated in the STEP file's own unit (it scales to mm only after), yet compared the 0.005 mm cap in file units.\n\n- **Measured on a new inch fixture.** `testdata/models/Milling-test-inch.step` is Milling-test.step with an INCH unit and every length divided by 25.4. Before the fix its Ø25 hole kept 0.02195 mm chords (448 facets), and the #689 bore was still refused as a 20.00 mm gouge. After the fix it gets 0.00492 mm on the Ø25 hole and 0.00495 mm on the R30 wall (952 facets, the same as the mm file).\n- **Fix.** The cap is now `MAX_CHORD / mm_per_unit`, the unit of each constant is stated, and the reduced-fidelity log prints mm and fires against the unfloored target.\n- **Metre files.** Before, the cap was 5 m and never bound (about 0.03 mm chords). Truck splits the metre sample into a non-manifold body at 5e-6 m (its weld tolerance is 1e-6 model units), so `MIN_TOL` is now 1e-5 file units. A metre file now reaches 0.01 mm and logs reduced fidelity. Millimetre and inch files are unaffected. Meshing in mm (scaling the B-rep first) belongs with #864.\n- **Pins.** `step_chord_units`: the inch chord error in mm is at most 0.005; a bore at the inch hole's own size posts clean; 0.05 mm oversize is refused. No mm test or golden moved.\n- **Gate.** The full quick gate is green on 9c5d869c (25.9 min). `import`, `bore_facet_sagitta`, `large_models`, `verify_arc_reading` and `step_chord_units` pass by name, and clippy is clean.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
